<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="d6a2b44f">&lt;p&gt;
    Run a small subset of test cases in the test environment and validate that the&amp;nbsp;expected results fulfill
    the&amp;nbsp;defined specifications. Examples of test cases that are performed to validate test environments include:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Confirm the requested test data is copied into the test environment
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Verify that security profiles&amp;nbsp;are similar to those in&amp;nbsp;production
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Verify the test environment has connectivity to other requested applications and can support the test execution on
        the requested operating system
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Assign the appropriate individuals proper access to the test environment
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Verify new enhancements are available in test environment for test execution
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Confirm that environment is stable and testable
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="e37de967"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="46d6b09f">&lt;p&gt;
    Examples of verification include:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Applications are working properly
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Users login credentials are available and valid
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Test data has been made available
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Required databases are connected and available
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="6e833c6f"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="985c8618">To verify environment suitability&amp;nbsp;for&amp;nbsp;validating that&amp;nbsp;solution behaviors fulfill solution requirements.</attribute>
